      "writtenOn": "2021-03-19T16:51:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think CONFIG_VBOOT_EFS2 flag is useful in this case. I uploaded patch which uses this flag. What about non-EFS2 boards that can pass power-on flag properly? Initially I thought that CONFIG_BOARD_RESET_AFTER_POWER_ON could be used, but this provides information if this is enabled now, not in old EC RO, on the other side this flag is relevant only in RO, so we can assume that if this is enabled now it will be enabled also in EC RO. What do you think?",
      "parentUuid": "8c8b8ea2_1e0eabdc",
      "revId": "510348ceb4608035dcd013000701de1787fa7613",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b1a0a49d_49304cab",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_tc_drp_acc_trysrc_sm.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 1530,
      "author": {
        "id": 1125984
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-03-23T03:07:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I would have expected CONFIG_BOARD_RESET_AFTER_POWER_ON to be set by default for all boards. Seems like it\u0027s easy to forget if that\u0027s not the case and I don\u0027t really see a reason why we _wouldn\u0027t_ that set due to Cr50 being present. If that then becomes the case, then it wouldn\u0027t be guaranteed that the RO has that config option.\n\nHowever, we could restrict that CONFIG_* option to be set only if SECTION_IS_RO.\n\nBut I think as of now, if it\u0027s enabled, we can assume it was enabled in RO.",
      "parentUuid": "ff24a4c1_7d31bcc0",
      "revId": "510348ceb4608035dcd013000701de1787fa7613",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
